                       "id":  "chunk-src-aeae4bf1-001",
                       "source_id":  "src-aeae4bf1",
                       "source_version":  "1.0.0",
                       "text":  "Rice Blast Symptoms in Paddies: Rice blast affects lowland paddy rice. Foliar lesions are diamond or spindle-shaped with greyish-white centers and brownish margins. Under humid flooded conditions, lesions coalesce, causing complete burning of the rice canopy. Paddy Water and Nitrogen Regulation: In tropical lowland paddies, avoid excessive split applications of urea nitrogen, which produces soft vegetative tissue highly vulnerable to blast penetration. Maintain continuous flooded water depth of 5 to",
                       "page_or_section":  "Section 1",
                       "crop_id":  "rice",
                       "region_id":  "tropical",
                       "growth_stage_id":  null,
                       "status":  "verified",
                       "relevance_score":  null,
                       "retrieval_mode":  null,
